          "guid": "msxt5okhxiaxtbx1",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source checkouts must preserve tsx when launching the synchronous download worker. The published path runs compiled JavaScript, but CI imports TypeScript with .js-to-.ts remapping; a plain child Node process could parse the file yet could not resolve its source-only imports, so every visual shard silently fell back to unsupported JavaScript Unicode classification.",
            "markdown": "Source checkouts must preserve tsx when launching the synchronous download worker. The published path runs compiled JavaScript, but CI imports TypeScript with .js-to-.ts remapping; a plain child Node process could parse the file yet could not resolve its source-only imports, so every visual shard silently fell back to unsupported JavaScript Unicode classification."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/icu-helper-acquire.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 122,
                  "endLine": 132,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const workerPath = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\n  // Source-checkout commands run this module through tsx.  A child launched as\n  // plain `node icu-helper-acquire.ts` loses tsx's .js→.ts import remapping\n  // (`./host-platform.js` is still source-only), while the published dist file\n  // is ordinary JavaScript and needs no loader.  Preserve the parent execution\n  // mode only for the source form.\n  const workerArgs = icuAcquireWorkerArgs(workerPath, target);\n  const proc = spawnSync(process.execPath, workerArgs, {\n    timeout: DOWNLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    encoding: \"utf8\",\n  });"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ],
            "ext-ai-tool-confidence": 0.99
          },
          "rank": 95,
